    {"question": "Single-story or multi-story for a Arkansas site?", "answer": "It depends on land cost and the submarket. Northwest Arkansas (Fayetteville-Springdale-Rogers) is the state's storage growth engine on Walmart, Tyson, and J.B. Hunt corporate expansion. Where land is affordable, single-story drive-up product builds fastest and cheapest; where land is dear, multi-story climate-controlled buildings stack the rentable square footage. We model both against the pro forma before the design is locked."}
